what is up everybody welcome back to the  cosmic wonder where we talk all things  marvel and mcu and if you thought that  doctor strange and the multiverse of  madness was pretty creepy well it was  actually supposed to be creepier than  what we saw that's right the original  script for doctor strange 2 was creepier  than what we saw on this screen and it  originally had a different villain now  most people know that doctor strange in  the multiverse of madness originally had  a different director scott derrickson he  directed the first doctor strange film  and was set to direct the second and he  really pushed for this to be marvel's  first horror movie he had a whole script  pretty much entirely done but from what  we know unfortunately there were a  little bit of creative differences  between him and marvel studios based on  him wanting it to be a lot more creepy  than kevin feige wanted it to be but we  recently found out a little bit about  that trashed script from the actual  doctor strange 2 writer michael waldron  including talks about who the villain  was and no it wasn't originally going to  be wanda we also have some news about  some scenes that took place in doctor  strange and the multiverse of madness  and how kevin feige wanted them in the  movie and these scenes connect to a  particular x-men one who actually had a  cut scene in multiverse of madness that  unfortunately we never saw and i'm sad  to say that that person was magneto i'm  sure everybody would have loved to have  seen him in the movie and would have  loved to see a connection between  magneto and wanda since there is a comic  storyline where magneto is wanda's  father so let's break down what the  original script was how the pandemic  affected it and what we could have  originally got which was an mcu where  the scarlet witch was not a villain so  let's dive into it and of course if  you're new be sure to subscribe so you  can stay up to date on all the latest  videos so i think a lot of people know  that nightmare was originally supposed  to be the villain for multiverse of  madness but i think a lot of people  thought that once sam raimi and michael  waldron got involved after scott  derrickson left that's when everything  changed however we have recently learned  that that wasn't exactly the case when  sam raimi originally came on he was  still working with the script that scott  derrickson made and nightmare was still  going to be the main villain however the  pandemic changed all of that and we  learned about this in a recent interview  with michael waldron he talked about how  they needed a more multiversal adversary  for doctor strange to face rather than  somebody like nightmare and this is how  the scarlet witch became the villain of  doctor strange 2. something that became  kind of controversial but here's what  michael waldron said in an interview  with den of geek when talking about the  original script he said there was  different stuff i think it's been  reported that once upon a time there was  some talk of nightmare and stuff like  that but when i came on board it was a  multiverse story and so it was always  about trying to figure out who that  multiversal adversary was going to be so  right away he says people heard about  nightmare being the original villain  however when he came on board they began  to talk about possibly changing the  villain to somebody who was more  multiversal he continues to say when i  originally came on in february of 2020  sam and i inherited the story that had  been worked on by scott derrickson and  jade bartlett the original writer on the  project it had a lot of really cool  ideas in it and we were initially going  to just try and figure out our version  of that story in time to start shooting  the movie in may then cove it happened a  month later and the movie was pushed  which afforded us an opportunity to kind  of start over and re-examine what we  wanted the movie to be so kovid was  actually responsible for doctor strange  2 getting pretty much completely  reworked originally the movie was  supposed to be about nightmare being the  villain and it would have some  multiversal aspects to it but covet  allowed michael waldron and sam raimi to  write a completely new script which i  think is good because i think the  multiverse is going to be a huge part of  the mcu moving forward and if we are  getting secret wars and maybe four years  from now which i hope we are we needed  the events of doctor strange 2 to happen  the way that they did we needed to see  spoiler alert the illuminati and we  needed to hear reed richards talk about  how incursions happen because that's how  secret wars happens universes collide  and this is what they wanted michael  waldron continues to say it meant that  steven would have had some real  experience with the multiverse by now  that he had been on a multiversal  adventure already this isn't his first  rodeo so to speak so that kind of  re-contextualizes the way you approach  all of this he understands the dangers  of it more now of course what he's  talking about here is spider-man no way  home he had just dealt with the  multiverse in no way home so he was  somewhat familiar with the multiverse  and the dangers that accompanied it but  originally this was supposed to come out  before no way home so they had to change  the script so the original script was  going to deal with nightmare but it was  also going to be doctor strange's first  dealings with the multiverse so if covet  wouldn't have happened we wouldn't have  gotten the illuminati which is probably  debatably the best part of multiverse of  madness even though the scarlet witch  wiped the floor with them so here's  where the big question comes in would it  have been better if we got the original  script for multiverse of madness we  would have had less multiverse  adventures but the scarlet witch would  not have been the villain and she would  still be a hero in the mcu her future  would have been totally different she  could have still been a part of the  avengers which now is kind of  questionable since of course wang is the  sorcerer supreme he might have a problem  with her joining the avengers when she  comes back because let's face it there's  no way she's dead strange and wong are  going to be keeping an eye out on her  probably pretty closely now i personally  really enjoyed seeing the scarlet witch  at her full power and even though i do  fully believe that she is returning how  she's going to return and what her  future is is very unknown right now so  let me know right now in the comments if  you would have liked her to not be the  villain and would have had her remain a  hero and keep in mind there's always  redemption for people it'll take some  really good writing but of course she  can return and still be a hero and now  to talk about a really interesting x-men  scene in multiverse of madness which  didn't actually involve the x-men it's  the scene where doctor strange and  america chavez travel through a bunch of  different universes in the span of what  20 seconds 40 seconds they visit a lot  of universes in that time frame and one  of them is the savage lands a tropical  jungle hidden in antarctica that's also  a prehistoric land because it has  dinosaurs in it but the biggest thing is  that at one point in time magneto claims  the land as his own and he builds a base  there and then the x-men come and they  battle it's a big storyline and the  savage lands is mostly connected with  magneto and the x-men and as it turns  out kevin feige the president of marvel  studios is actually the person who's  said to put this in the movie in a  recent interview with the visual effects  team they told us about kevin feige  wanting the savage lands in the movie  when they said they proposed a jungle  and kevin feige said well it would be  cool if it was savage world so they put  it in the movie at kevin feige's request  we also got word that there was a  deleted scene with magneto the deleted  scene apparently showed him as wanda's  father in this universe the earth-838  universe once the illuminati learned  about dreamwalking and what the scarlet  witch could do they wanted to perform a  lobotomy on the scarlet witch of that  universe to make sure she wasn't ever  strong enough to dreamwalk but they had  to consult with her father magneto first  so that was supposed to be in the film  and now we know that kevin feige wanted  the savage world in multiverse of  madness a place that is heavily related  to the x-men now in 2019 kevin feige  announced that the x-men or mutants were  coming pretty soon he also announced  that the fantastic four were coming  pretty soon and we got reed richards and  multiverse of madness so i'm assuming  and hoping that the x-men are coming  sooner than later in the marvel  cinematic universe hopefully within the  next couple of years i'm also hoping  that we get the cosmic entities in the  mcu pretty soon and it's looking like  that might actually be the case you may  have also noticed that one of the  universes that they go through is a  universe where we can see the living  tribunal and as it turns out that was  also at the request of kevin feige when  the visual effects team was talking  about the worlds and universes they  created they said one was an incan  statue world which ended up in the movie  because kevin feige thought well that  could be a great world to put the living  tribunal in so that world became the  living tribunal world now for those of  you who may not be aware the living  tribunal is a cosmic entity that watches  over the entire multiverse and when  things get too crazy crazier than what  we saw in multiverse of madness he steps  in and he judges people based on their  crimes against the multiverse but here's  the catch he has three heads and they  all have to agree unanimously on the  judgment so if you're wondering why  hasn't the living tribunal stepped in  yet it could be because one well maybe  something wasn't that big to interfere  with yet or two maybe all of the heads  didn't agree because again it has to be  unanimous but we've now seen several  mentions and hints of the living  tribunal in the mcu in the first doctor  strange mordo mentioned the living  tribunal we saw a statue of the living  tribunal's head in loki then we saw him  in the recent doctor strange film and we  recently saw a statue of the living  tribunal's head and other cosmic  entities in the trailer for thor love  and thunder so i'm hoping that the  cosmic entities are about to become a  thing in the mcu they play a major role  in the comics and it's looking like  they're about to play a major role in  the mcu and since thor love and thunder  is going to explore other gods i'm  hoping they take that opportunity to at  least talk about cosmic entities so  that's it for all the latest news today  about multiverse of madness be sure to  let me know if you think wanda should  have remained a hero or do you like what  happened in multiverse of madness leave  your thoughts down below in the comments  and don't forget to like this video and  subscribe to stay up to date on all of  the latest videos of course for live  updates you can follow me on instagram  and twitter and as always thank you all  so much for watching woof

